%% CAO — full system sequence diagram
%% Three phases: INSTALL (once) -> APPLY (after every config/prompt edit) -> RUNTIME (each cao-run).
%% This is the contract map: who calls whom, what file each step reads/writes, where quota/fallback branches.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as You (human)
    participant BS as bootstrap.sh<br/>(1_install)
    participant CFG as cao.config.local.toml<br/>(2_configure, gitignored)
    participant PR as prompts/.md files<br/>(2_configure)
    participant RC as render_config.py<br/>(3_apply)
    participant AP as apply.sh<br/>(3_apply)
    participant STG as agent_store (_)<br/>STAGING
    participant CAO as cao CLI + DB<br/>agent-store (-) CANONICAL
    participant OCJ as opencode.json<br/>(~/.aws/opencode)
    participant DR as cao-doctor<br/>(run)
    participant RUN as cao-run<br/>(run)
    participant SRV as cao-server<br/>(daemon :9889)
    participant TMUX as tmux sessions
    participant SUP as supervisor<br/>(claude, Tech Lead)
    participant W as workers<br/>(coder/analyst/codex/qa/claude)
    participant EP as nitec endpoint<br/>llm.nitec.kz/v1
    participant TOK as cao-tokens<br/>(run)

    Note over U,CAO: ===== PHASE 1 — INSTALL (once, idempotent) =====
    U->>BS: ./bootstrap.sh (--inherit-mcp) (--with-kodeks)
    BS->>BS: install prereqs (uv, tmux, node), CAO, worker CLIs (claude/codex/opencode/agy)
    BS->>STG: mkdir agent_store, copy prompts .md files
    BS->>CAO: cao install staging .md files  (registers into canonical agent-store + DB)
    BS->>BS: patch pyte (agy ANSI fix) · skip agy onboarding · neutralize codex hooks
    BS-->>U: prints INTERACTIVE login steps (claude /login, codex login, agy)

    Note over U,OCJ: ===== PHASE 2 — APPLY (after editing config or prompts) =====
    U->>CFG: edit workers/roles/models (single source of truth)
    U->>PR: edit prompt bodies (execution rules)
    U->>AP: ./apply.sh
    AP->>RC: render_config.py
    RC->>CFG: read (local overrides template)
    RC->>OCJ: write provider=nitec + models(deepseek,kimi,glm) + default
    RC->>STG: write each worker .md (provider/model into frontmatter)
    RC->>STG: regen supervisor AUTO-MAPPING from aliases+focus
    RC->>STG: prune_stale_profiles — delete staging .md with no tracked source
    Note right of RC: GAP: prune cleans STAGING only,<br/>not canonical agent-store (-).<br/>Rename also needs `cao profile remove`.
    AP->>CAO: cao install staging «p».md  for each registered profile
    CAO->>CAO: copy STAGING → canonical agent-store (-) + update DB
    AP-->>U: offer cao-server restart (picks up new configs)

    Note over U,EP: ===== PHASE 3 — RUNTIME (each cao-run) =====
    U->>RUN: cao-run
    RUN->>DR: pre-flight (unless --skip-check)
    DR->>DR: D1 toolchain, D2 engines, D3 logins, D4 endpoint reachable
    DR->>EP: GET /models (auth LOCAL_API_KEY) → 200?
    alt claude logged out / unavailable
        DR->>DR: write ~/.cao/supervisor_provider = fallback (antigravity_cli)
    else claude ok
        DR->>DR: clear stale ~/.cao/supervisor_provider
    end
    DR-->>RUN: exit 0 (ready) or non-zero (abort)
    RUN->>RUN: pick supervisor provider:<br/>env CAO_SUPERVISOR_PROVIDER, then hint file, then claude_code
    RUN->>SRV: start cao-server if :9889 not listening (passes LOCAL_API_KEY)
    RUN->>TMUX: tmux setenv -g LOCAL_API_KEY (so opencode panes inherit)
    RUN->>CAO: cao launch --agents code_supervisor --provider «chosen» --auto-approve
    alt primary=claude_code AND launch fails (quota burned)
        RUN->>CAO: auto-retry once on fallback (antigravity_cli / codex)
    end
    CAO->>TMUX: spawn supervisor session (cao-supervisor)
    TMUX->>SUP: boot claude with cao-mcp-server MCP (assign, send_message tools)

    Note over SUP,W: ---- supervisor orchestration loop ----
    U->>SUP: describe task
    SUP->>SUP: size it (small change → delegate · big → design first)
    opt big feature / new project
        SUP->>W: assign analyst_worker (Gemini): map repo / read long docs / images
        W-->>SUP: compact map with path:line anchors
        SUP->>SUP: design + write Mermaid to cao_session/design/, get human approval
        SUP->>SUP: derive tasks.json (engine per task from mapping)
    end
    SUP->>W: assign ready tasks in parallel (assign MCP tool, up to max_concurrent_workers)
    CAO->>TMUX: spawn worker panes per profile
    W->>EP: coder_worker → nitec/deepseek (bulk impl)
    W->>W: codex_worker → UI · claude_worker → contracts/hard logic
    W-->>SUP: send_message result back (via caller terminal_id)
    SUP->>W: audit gate: assign antigravity_worker (QA)
    W-->>SUP: reports/audit.md + BLOCKER? summary
    alt blockers
        SUP->>W: fix-task to OWNER (coder fixes own · claude fixes contract)
        SUP->>W: re-audit until clean
    end
    SUP-->>U: session complete · you run acceptance pass

    Note over U,TOK: ===== OBSERVABILITY (any time) =====
    U->>TOK: cao-tokens (--daily|--heatmap|--cao-only|--day)
    TOK->>TOK: scrape ~/.claude jsonl + codex/opencode sqlite (local, no billing API)
    TOK-->>U: per-engine / per-day / heatmap · --cao-only isolates cao from all-claude
    U->>RUN: cao-stop (shutdown) when done — workers survive detach otherwise
